# clinical v1.16 — a clinical:EncounterParticipant on its own.
#
# WHY A STANDALONE NODE IS A SEPARATE FIXTURE.
# clinical:EncounterParticipantShape carries sh:targetClass, not a reachability
# rule, so it constrains a participation wherever one appears. Validating one
# only as a child of an encounter would leave that untested, and Cascade pods
# are validated FILE BY FILE: a participation written to a different file from
# its encounter must still be checked, and under per-file validation it arrives
# exactly like this, with nothing pointing at it.
#
# It carries no encounter reference for the same reason. Adding one would make
# the fixture depend on a node that is not here, which is the shape of a
# cross-file edge the v1.11 ruling deliberately stopped constraining.
#
# WHAT PASSES HERE AND WHY THAT IS THE CLAIM. The shape requires NO field:
# FHIR makes every sub-element of Encounter.participant optional
# (participant.type 0..*, participant.individual 0..1), so a minCount would fail
# conformant source data. What it does check is cardinality and datatype, so
# that a participation cannot carry two names or two specialties -- which is
# where a merge of two records silently corrupts one. This node carries one of
# each and passes; its INVALID twin carries two names and does not.
#
# The role code is repeated because Encounter.participant.type is 0..*, and the
# second code is a LOCAL one: an extensible binding means a server may send a
# code from outside encounter-participant-type and still be conformant, and the
# shape binds no value set precisely so that code is kept rather than dropped.
#
# The node is an IRI here, but the shape does not require one: unlike an
# Encounter, nothing points at a participation from another file, so a blank
# node a serializer writes for a structural sub-node is legal.
#
# Fully synthetic.

@prefix clinical: <https://ns.cascadeprotocol.org/clinical/v1#> .

<urn:uuid:e0c00116-0000-4000-8000-000000000010> a clinical:EncounterParticipant ;
    clinical:participantName "Priya Nandakumar, NP" ;
    clinical:participantRole "primary performer" ;
    clinical:participantRoleCode "PPRF" ;
    clinical:participantRoleCode "MRD-ROLE-NP" ;
    clinical:participantSpecialty "Nurse Practitioner, Acute Care" .
